ent, kept unescaped.\n  SoupStrainer(name=None, attrs={}, string=None, **kwargs) — bs4's name/attribute/string filter, shared by find_* and parse_only.\n  StopParsing(...) — Raised internally to abandon a parse; catch it only if you drive the builder yourself.\n  Stylesheet(value) — The string inside a `<style>` element, kept unescaped.\n  Tag(parser=None, builder=None, name=None, namespace=None, prefix=None, attrs=None, parent=None, previous=None, is_xml=None, sourceline=None, sourcepos=None, can_be_empty_element=None, cdata_list_attributes=None, preserve_whitespace_tags=None, interesting_string_types=None, namespaces=None) — One element of the tree: attributes by `tag[\"href\"]`, children by `.contents`, and the w…\n  TemplateString(value) — A string inside a `<template>` element.\n  UnicodeDammit(markup, known_definite_encodings=[], smart_quotes_to=None, is_html=False, exclude_encodings=[], user_encodings=None, override_encodings=None) — bs4.dammit.UnicodeDammit: bytes in, str out, plus the encoding it guessed.\n  XMLParsedAsHTMLWarning(...) — Warns that XML markup is being parsed with the HTML parser.\n\nModules:\n  builder — Tree builders and their registry; only the html.parser builder is real in this shim.\n  css — The CSS entry point behind `soup.select`, delegating to the bundled soupsieve engine.\n  dammit — Encoding detection (UnicodeDammit). No chardet or charset-normalizer here, so it is upst…\n  diagnose — Parser diagnostics — `diagnose(markup)` prints how this shim reads a document.\n  element — Node classes of the tree — Tag, NavigableString, Comment and the other string types.\n  formatter — Output formatters: how attributes and entities are written back out by `str(soup)` and `…\n\nData:\n  DEFAULT_OUTPUT_ENCODING\n  PYTHON_SPECIFIC_ENCODINGS\n  builder_registry\n\nRead one member: doc(\"bs4.BeautifulSoup\")"}
