 {:name "dateutil", :kind "module", :text "`dateutil.tz`, `dateutil.parser`, `dateutil.relativedelta`, `rrule`, `easter` and `utils` over the JVM zone database. Other dateutil submodules are not supported. Part of the vis time shim; see `doc(\"tzdata\")`.\n\nModules:\n  easter — dateutil.easter: easter(year) computes the Gregorian Easter date.\n  parser — dateutil.parser: parse(timestr) reads an ISO-8601 or common date string into a datetime.\n  relativedelta — dateutil.relativedelta: relativedelta arithmetic — add months, years or weekday offsets …\n  rrule — dateutil.rrule: rrule recurrence rules — DAILY/WEEKLY/MONTHLY/YEARLY iteration over date…\n  tz — dateutil.tz: gettz, tzutc, tzlocal and tzoffset time zones over the JVM zone database.\n  utils — dateutil.utils: today() and small datetime conveniences over the shim's tz support.\n  zoneinfo — dateutil.zoneinfo: gettz-style zone lookup backed by the JVM time-zone database.\n\nRead one member: doc(\"dateutil.easter\")"}
