se`.\n  get(url, **kw) — Send a GET request and return a `Response`: `httpx.get(url, params=..., headers=...)`.\n  head(url, **kw) — Send a HEAD request and return a `Response` (no body).\n  options(url, **kw) — Send an OPTIONS request and return a `Response`.\n  patch(url, **kw) — Send a PATCH request with `content`/`data`/`json` and return a `Response`.\n  post(url, **kw) — Send a POST request with `content`, `data`, `json` or `files` and return a `Response`.\n  put(url, **kw) — Send a PUT request with `content`/`data`/`json` and return a `Response`.\n  request(method, url, **kw) — Send one request by method name without keeping a client: `httpx.request('GET', url)`.\n  stream(method, url, **kw) — Open a streaming response context: `with httpx.stream('GET', url) as r:`. The body is re…\n\nRead one member: doc(\"httpx.AsyncClient\")"}
