 {:name "nippy.dumps", :kind "function", :text "Serialize plain Python data to Vis Nippy bytes the Clojure host reads back.", :call "dumps(value)"}
 {:name "nippy.encode", :kind "function", :text "Serialize plain Python data to Vis Nippy bytes the Clojure host reads back.", :call "encode(value)"}
 {:name "nippy.loads", :kind "function", :text "Read trusted Vis Nippy bytes (or their base64 text) back into plain Python data.", :call "loads(data)"}
 {:name "nippy_decode", :kind "function", :text "Read trusted Vis Nippy bytes (or their base64 text) back into plain Python data.\n\nVectorz vectors arrive as lists and Clojure's exact types are not preserved.\nRaises TypeError on a non-bytes argument, NippyError on malformed input.\nNever decode bytes from an untrusted source.", :call "nippy_decode(data)"}
 {:name "nippy_encode", :kind "function", :text "Serialize plain Python data to Vis Nippy bytes the Clojure host reads back.\n\nTakes what JSON takes plus bytes, and answers `bytes`. Raises NippyError on a\nvalue the encoder cannot represent.", :call "nippy_encode(value)"}
 {:name "numpy", :kind "module", :text "Pure-Python `numpy` subset: ndarray, broadcasting, reductions, `linalg` (norm/det/inv/solve/eig/svd/qr/lstsq), random, histogram. No C speed and no shared-memory views. `numpy.fft` transforms, `pad` beyond 1-D and axis `cumsum`/`flip` beyond 1-D raise `NotImplementedError`.\n\nClasses:\n  dtype(name) — Element type of an ndarray (float64, int64, bool_), exposed as `numpy.dtype`.\n  ndarray(data, shape, dtype) — Dense N-dimensional array of Python numbers: shape, dtype, slicing, broadcasting arithme…\n\nFunctions:\n  abs(a) — Elementwise absolute value (also exported as `abs` and `fabs`).\n  absolute(a) — Elementwise absolute value (also exported as `abs` and `fabs`).\n  add(a, b) — Elementwise sum of two arrays, with broadcasting.\n  all(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — True when every element is truthy, over an axis or the whole array.\n  allclose(a, b, rtol=1e-05, atol=1e-08) — True when two arrays agree everywhere within a tolerance.\n  amax(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — Largest element, over an axis or the whole array (also exported as `max`).\n  amin(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — Smallest element, over an axis or the whole array (also exported as `min`).\n  any(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — True when at least one element is truthy, over an axis or the whole array.\n  arange(*args, dtype=None) — Evenly spaced values over a half-open range, like `range` with floats.\n  arccos(a) — Elementwise inverse cosine, in radians.\n  arcsin(a) — Elementwise inverse sine, in radians.\n  arctan(a) — Elementwise inverse tangent, in radians.\n  arctan2(y, x) — Elementwise inverse tangent of y/x, using the signs to pick the quadrant.\n  argmax(a, axis=None) — Index of the largest element.\n  argmin(a, axis=None) — Index of the smallest element.\n  argsort(a) — Indices that would sort the array.\n  around(a, decimals=0) — Round to the given number of decimals (also exported as `round` and `round_`).\n  array(obj, dtype=None, copy=True, ndmin=0) — Build an ndarray from nested sequences, copying by default.\n  array_equal(a, b) — True when two arrays have the same shape and the same elements.\n  array_split(a, indices_or_sections, axis=0) — Split an array into parts along an axis, allowing an uneven last part.\n  asarray(obj, dtype=None) — Return the input as an ndarray, without copying when it already is one.\n  atleast_3d(a) — Return the input with at least three dimensions.\n  broadcast_to(a, shape) — View the input as if it had the given broadcast shape.\n  ceil(a) — Elementwise round up to an integer.\n  clip(a, a_min, a_max) — Limit values to the interval [a_min, a_max].\n  column_stack(arrays) — Stack 1-D arrays as the columns of a 2-D array.\n  concatenate(arrays, axis=0) — Join a sequence of arrays along an existing axis.\n  corrcoef(m, y=None) — Pearson correlation coefficient matrix of the rows.\n  cos(a) — Elementwise cosine, in radians.\n  cosh(a) — Elementwise hyperbolic cosine.\n  count_nonzero(a) — How many elements are not zero.\n  cov(m, y=None, ddof=1) — Covariance matrix of the rows.\n  cross(a, b) — Cross product of two 3-vectors.\n  cumprod(a, axis=None) — Running product along an axis.\n  cumsum(a, axis=None) — Running total along an axis.\n  deg2rad(a) — Convert degrees to radians (also exported as `deg2rad`).\n  degrees(a) — Convert radians to degrees (also exported as `rad2deg`).\n  diag(v, k=0) — Extract a diagonal from a matrix, or build a matrix from a diagonal vector.\n  diff(a, n=1) — Differences between neighbouring elements along an axis.\n  divide(a, b) — Elementwise true division (also exported as `true_divide`).\n  dot(a, b) — Dot product: inner product for vectors, matrix product for 2-D (also `inner`).\n  dstack(arrays) — Stack arrays along the third axis.\n  empty(shape, dtype=None) — New array of the given shape, contents unspecified (this shim fills it with 0).\n  empty_like(a, dtype=None) — Uninitialized array with the same shape as the input.\n  exp(a) — Elementwise e**x.\n  expand_dims(a, axis) — Insert a new axis of length one at the given position.\n  eye(n, m=None, k=0, dtype=None) — Two-dimensional array with ones on a diagonal and zeros elsewhere.\n  fabs(a) — Elementwise absolute value (also exported as `abs` and `fabs`).\n  flip(a, axis=None) — Reverse the order of elements along an axis.\n  floor(a) — Elementwise round down to an integer.\n  floor_divide(a, b) — Elementwise floor division, the `//` operator.\n  fmax(a, b) — Elementwise larger of two arrays, ignoring NaN.\n  fmin(a, b) — Elementwise smaller of two arrays, ignoring NaN.\n  full(shape, fill_value, dtype=None) — New array of the given shape filled with one value.\n  full_like(a, fill_value, dtype=None) — Array of the same shape as the input, filled with one value.\n  gradient(a, spacing=1.0) — Central-difference numerical gradient of a sampled function.\n  histogram(a, bins=10, range=None) — Counts per bin and the bin edges of a data set.\n  hstack(arrays) — Stack arrays column-wise (along the second axis, or the first for 1-D).\n  hypot(a, b) — Elementwise Euclidean distance sqrt(x**2 + y**2).\n  identity(n, dtype=None) — Square identity matrix of size n.\n  inner(a, b) — Dot product: inner product for vectors, matrix product for 2-D (also `inner`).\n  interp(x, xp, fp) — Piecewise-linear interpolation of a one-dimensional sampled function.\n  isclose(a, b, rtol=1e-05, atol=1e-08) — Elementwise test that two arrays agree within a tolerance.\n  isfinite(a) — Elementwise test for a finite number.\n  isinf(a) — Elementwise test for positive or negative infinity.\n  isnan(a) — Elementwise test for NaN.\n  isscalar(x) — True when the value is a single number or string, not an array or sequence.\n  linspace(start, stop, num=50, endpoint=True, dtype=None) — `num` evenly spaced samples from `start` to `stop`, endpoint included.\n  log(a) — Elementwise natural logarithm.\n  log10(a) — Elementwise base-10 logarithm.\n  log2(a) — Elementwise base-2 logarithm.\n  logaddexp(a, b) — Elementwise log(exp(x) + exp(y)), computed without overflow.\n  logical_and(a, b) — Elementwise boolean AND.\n  logical_not(a) — Elementwise boolean NOT.\n  logical_or(a, b) — Elementwise boolean OR.\n  logical_xor(a, b) — Elementwise boolean exclusive OR.\n  matmul(a, b) — Matrix product, the `@` operator.\n  max(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — Largest element, over an axis or the whole array (also exported as `max`).\n  maximum(a, b) — Elementwise larger of two arrays.\n  mean(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — Arithmetic mean, over an axis or the whole array.\n  median(a, axis=None) — Middle value, over an axis or the whole array.\n  meshgrid(x, y) — Coordinate matrices from coordinate vectors.\n  min(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — Smallest element, over an axis or the whole array (also exported as `min`).\n  minimum(a, b) — Elementwise smaller of two arrays.\n  mod(a, b) — Elementwise remainder with the sign of the divisor (also exported as `mod`).\n  multiply(a, b) — Elementwise product of two arrays, with broadcasting.\n  nanmax(a, axis=None) — Largest element, ignoring NaN.\n  nanmean(a, axis=None) — Mean of elements, ignoring NaN.\n  nanmin(a, axis=None) — Smallest element, ignoring NaN.\n  nanstd(a, axis=None) — Standard deviation, ignoring NaN.\n  nansum(a, axis=None) — Sum of elements, ignoring NaN.\n  ndim(a) — How many dimensions an array-like has.\n  nonzero(a) — Indices of the elements that are not zero.\n  ones(shape, dtype=None) — New array of the given shape filled with 1.\n  ones_like(a, dtype=None) — Array of ones with the same shape as the input.\n  outer(a, b) — Outer product of two vectors.\n  pad(a, pad_width, mode='constant', constant_values=0) — Pad an array at both ends of an axis.\n  percentile(a, q, axis=None) — Value below which the given percentage of the data falls.\n  polyfit(x, y, deg) — Least-squares fit of a polynomial of the given degree.\n  polyval(p, x) — Evaluate a polynomial, highest power first, at the given points.\n  power(a, b) — Elementwise exponentiation.\n  prod(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — Product of elements, over an axis or the whole array.\n  quantile(a, q, axis=None) — Value below which the given fraction of the data falls.\n  rad2deg(a) — Convert radians to degrees (also exported as `rad2deg`).\n  radians(a) — Convert degrees to radians (also exported as `deg2rad`).\n  ravel(a) — Flatten to one dimension.\n  reciprocal(a) — Elementwise 1/x.\n  remainder(a, b) — Elementwise remainder with the sign of the divisor (also exported as `mod`).\n  repeat(a, repeats, axis=None) — Repeat each element the given number of times.\n  reshape(a, newshape) — Same data, new shape; one dimension may be -1 to be inferred.\n  rint(a) — Elementwise round to the nearest integer.\n  roll(a, shift, axis=None) — Shift elements along an axis, wrapping around the end.\n  round(a, decimals=0) — Round to the given number of decimals (also exported as `round` and `round_`).\n  round_(a, decimals=0) — Round to the given number of decimals (also exported as `round` and `round_`).\n  shape(a) — The length of an array-like along each of its dimensions, as a tuple.\n  sign(a) — Elementwise sign: -1, 0 or 1.\n  sin(a) — Elementwise sine, in radians.\n  sinh(a) — Elementwise hyperbolic sine.\n  size(a) — How many elements an array-like holds in total.\n  sort(a, axis=-1) — Return a sorted copy along an axis.\n  split(a, indices_or_sections, axis=0) — Split an array into equal parts along an axis.\n  sqrt(a) — Elementwise square root.\n  square(a) — Elementwise square.\n  squeeze(a, axis=None) — Drop axes of length one.\n  stack(arrays, axis=0) — Join a sequence of arrays along a NEW axis.\n  std(a, axis=None, ddof=0, keepdims=False) — Standard deviation, over an axis or the whole array.\n  subtract(a, b) — Elementwise difference of two arrays, with broadcasting.\n  sum(a, axis=None, keepdims=False) — Sum of elements, over an axis or the whole array.\n  take(a, indices, axis=None) — Select elements along an axis by integer index.\n  tan(a) — Elementwise tangent, in radians.\n  tanh(a) — Elementwise hyperbolic tangent.\n  tile(a, reps) — Repeat the whole array to build a larger one.\n  trace(a) — Sum along the main diagonal.\n  transpose(a, axes=None) — Permute the axes of an array; for 2-D, the matrix transpose.\n  true_divide(a, b) — Elementwise true division (also exported as `true_divide`).\n  trunc(a) — Elementwise round toward zero.\n  unique(a, return_counts=False) — Sorted unique values of an array.\n  var(a, axis=None, ddof=0, keepdims=False) — Variance, over an axis or the whole array.\n  vstack(arrays) — Stack arrays row-wise (along the first axis).\n  where(cond, x=None, y=None) — Choose elementwise between two arrays by a boolean condition, or find true indices.\n  zeros(shape, dtype=None) — New array of the given shape filled with 0.\n  zeros_like(a, dtype=None) — Array of zeros with the same shape as the input.\n\nModules:\n  fft — Only the frequency helpers are real here: fftfreq and rfftfreq. Every transform (fft, if…\n  linalg — Dense linear algebra on 2-D arrays: norm, det, inv, solve, matrix_power, matrix_rank, ei…\n  ma — Masked arrays: MaskedArray, masked_array, getdata/getmask/getmaskarray, isMaskedArray.\n  polynomial — The `Polynomial` class: build one from coefficients, call it to evaluate.\n  random — Seedable pseudo-random numbers: default_rng, RandomState/Generator, random_sample, ranf.\n  testing — Array assertions for tests: assert_allclose, assert_array_equal, assert_equal.\n  typing — Annotation aliases only: `ArrayLike` and `NDArray` accept a subscript and check nothing.\n\nData:\n  Inf\n  NaN\n  e\n  euler_gamma\n  inf\n  nan\n  newaxis\n  pi\n\nRead one member: doc(\"numpy.Inf\")"}
