 {:name "pandas", :kind "module", :text "Pure-Python `pandas` subset: Series, DataFrame, groupby, merge, `read_csv`. No C speed or vectorized IO-heavy APIs; `to_csv(path)` is disabled — use `to_csv()` for text.\n\nClasses:\n  DataFrame(data=None, columns=None, index=None) — Two-dimensional labelled table - dict-of-columns construction, `[]`/`loc`/`iloc` selecti…\n  Index(data=(), name=None, dtype=None) — A labelled axis: a sequence of labels carrying a `name`.\n  Series(data=None, index=None, name=None, dtype=None) — One-dimensional labelled column - elementwise arithmetic, boolean masking, value_counts,…\n\nFunctions:\n  concat(objs, axis=0, ignore_index=False) — Concatenate DataFrames along an axis into one frame, optionally renumbering the index.\n  crosstab(rows, cols) — Count how often two label sequences co-occur, as a frequency table.\n  date_range(start=None, end=None, periods=None, freq='D') — Evenly spaced timestamps from start/end/periods at frequency `freq`.\n  isna(x) — True where a value is missing; a Series or DataFrame answers elementwise.\n  isnull(x) — True where a value is missing; a Series or DataFrame answers elementwise.\n  merge(left, right, **kw) — Join two DataFrames on their shared or named columns - the function form of DataFrame.me…\n  notna(x) — True where a value is present - the negation of isna.\n  notnull(x) — True where a value is present - the negation of isna.\n  pivot_table(data, values=None, index=None, columns=None, aggfunc='mean', fill_value=None) — Aggregate long data into a wide table of `index` by `columns`, one aggfunc per cell.\n  read_csv(path_or_buf, sep=None, header='infer') — Read a CSV file or buffer into a DataFrame, inferring the header row and the separator.\n  read_json(s, orient='records') — Read a JSON string into a DataFrame; `orient` selects the record layout.\n  to_datetime(arg, format=None, errors='raise') — Parse values into datetimes; `format` pins the layout, `errors='coerce'` yields NA.\n  to_numeric(s, errors='raise') — Coerce values to float; `errors='coerce'` turns what will not parse into NA.\n  unique(vals) — The distinct values of a sequence, in first-seen order.\n\nModules:\n  api — pandas.api - dtype predicates under `pandas.api.types`: is_numeric_dtype, is_integer_dty…\n  plotting — pandas.plotting - accepted so imports succeed; scatter_matrix draws nothing and register…\n  testing — pandas.testing - assert_frame_equal and assert_series_equal for comparing results in a t…\n  tseries — pandas.tseries - offsets only; `offsets.Day(n)` is a timedelta of n days.\n\nData:\n  NA\n  NaN\n\nRead one member: doc(\"pandas.DataFrame\")"}
