 {:name "paramiko", :kind "module", :text "Paramiko-compatible SSH2 over pure-Java JSch: `SSHClient` `exec_command`/SFTP, RSA/DSS/ECDSA/Ed25519 keys, plus a MINA-backed server side for reverse forwards (`doc(\"paramiko\")`). Not supported: `invoke_shell` — use `exec_command`/SFTP.\n\nClasses:\n  Agent() — The running ssh-agent seen through SSH_AUTH_SOCK — get_keys() lends them to a connection.\n  AgentKey(agent=None, blob=b'', comment='', **kw) — One key the running ssh-agent holds, usable for publickey auth without its private half.\n  AuthenticationException(...) — Authentication was refused — wrong password, wrong key, or no accepted method.\n  AutoAddPolicy() — Accept an unknown host key and remember it. Convenient; trusts the first connection.\n  BadAuthenticationType(explanation='', types=None) — The server refused the method tried and named the ones it does allow.\n  BadHostKeyException(hostname=None, got_key=None, expected_key=None) — The host key the server presented is not the one known_hosts records.\n  BufferedFile() — Base of the channel and SFTP file objects — buffered read/write with a context manager.\n  Channel(code) — One multiplexed channel over a Transport: send/recv bytes, exec a command, close it.\n  ChannelException(code=0, text='') — The channel could not be opened, or the server closed it with a failure code.\n  ChannelFile(data, channel) — The stdout of a channel as a file object — what exec_command() returns second.\n  ChannelStderrFile(data, channel) — The stderr of a channel as a file object — what exec_command() returns third.\n  ChannelStdinFile() — The stdin of a channel as a writable file object — exec_command()'s first return.\n  ConfigParseError(...) — The ssh_config text could not be parsed.\n  CouldNotCanonicalize(...) — Hostname canonicalization asked for by the config could not be completed.\n  DSSKey(path=None, password=None, _data=None) — A DSA (ssh-dss) key. Accepted for compatibility; most current servers refuse the algorit…\n  ECDSAKey(path=None, password=None, _data=None) — An ECDSA (NIST P-curve) key — from_private_key_file(path) or generate().\n  Ed25519Key(path=None, password=None, _data=None, **kw) — An Ed25519 key — the default modern host and user key type.\n  HostKeys(filename=None) — A known_hosts database — load, add, lookup, save; what a MissingHostKeyPolicy decides on.\n  IncompatiblePeer(...) — The peer offers no algorithm in common — no shared kex, cipher, MAC or host key type.\n  InteractiveQuery(name='', instructions='', *prompts) — Server side: the prompt set returned by keyboard-interactive authentication.\n  Message(content=None) — An SSH wire message being built or read — get_/add_ one typed field at a time.\n  MessageOrderError(...) — A protocol message arrived out of the order the SSH state machine allows.\n  MissingHostKeyPolicy() — Base policy for an unknown host key — subclass and implement missing_host_key().\n  NoValidConnectionsError(errors=None) — Every candidate address for that host refused the connection.\n  PKey(path=None, password=None, _data=None) — Base of every key type: from_private_key_file/from_private_key, generate, get_fingerprint.\n  PasswordRequiredException(...) — The private key is encrypted and no passphrase was given to load it.\n  ProxyCommand(command_line) — A local command used as the transport socket — ProxyCommand from an ssh_config.\n  ProxyCommandFailure(...) — The ProxyCommand process failed or closed before the session was up.\n  PublicBlob(type_, blob, comment=None) — A raw public-key blob (an OpenSSH certificate or `.pub` body), from_string/from_file.\n  RSAKey(path=None, password=None, _data=None) — An RSA private or public key — from_private_key_file(path, password=None) or generate(bi…\n  RejectPolicy() — Refuse to connect to a host whose key is not already known. The safe default.\n  SFTP(handle) — SFTP over an open Transport: listdir, stat, open, get/put, mkdir, remove, rename.\n  SFTPAttributes() — Stat of one remote path: st_size, st_uid, st_gid, st_mode, st_atime, st_mtime.\n  SFTPClient(handle) — SFTP over an open Transport: listdir, stat, open, get/put, mkdir, remove, rename.\n  SFTPError(...) — SFTP protocol failure — a bad handle, a refused operation, a malformed packet.\n  SFTPFile(sftp, path, mode='r') — One remote file opened over SFTP — read/write/seek/close, and a context manager.\n  SFTPHandle(flags=0) — Server side: one open file a SFTPServerInterface handed back — read/write/stat/chattr.\n  SFTPServer(channel, name, server, sftp_si=None, *larg, **kwarg) — Server side: the SFTP subsystem itself, driving one SFTPServerInterface per session.\n  SFTPServerInterface(server, *larg, **kwarg) — Server side: subclass this to serve SFTP — open, list_folder, stat, remove, rename.\n  SSHClient() — High-level SSH connection: connect(), exec_command(), open_sftp(). No invoke_shell here.\n  SSHConfig() — A parsed ssh_config — from_path/from_text, then lookup(host) for the effective options.\n  SSHConfigDict(...) — The dict SSHConfig.lookup answers, with as_bool/as_int readers for its string values.\n  SSHException(...) — Base of every paramiko failure; catch this to catch any SSH error from this shim.\n  SecurityOptions(transport=None) — The negotiated algorithm preferences of a Transport — ciphers, macs, keys, kex.\n  ServerInterface() — Server side: subclass to answer auth and channel requests for an incoming session.\n  SubsystemHandler(channel, name, server, *larg, **kwarg) — Server side: base of a named subsystem handler, which is how SFTP is served.\n  Transport(sock=None, sess=None) — The negotiated SSH session under a client: open_session(), open_sftp_client(), forwarding.\n  UnknownKeyType(key_type=None, key_bytes=None) — The key type in this file or blob is not one this shim knows how to load.\n  WarningPolicy() — Accept an unknown host key but log a warning instead of storing it.\n\nModules:\n  agent — Agent and AgentKey — the keys a running ssh-agent lends over SSH_AUTH_SOCK.\n  channel — Channel and its file wrappers — stdin, stdout and stderr of one exec_command.\n  client — SSHClient and the host-key policies (AutoAdd, Reject, Warning) live here.\n  common — Protocol constants: auth and open failure codes, message numbers, log levels.\n  config — SSHConfig, SSHConfigDict and the errors raised while parsing an ssh_config.\n  ecdsakey — ECDSAKey — ECDSA (NIST P-curve) keys.\n  ed25519key — Ed25519Key — Ed25519 private and public keys.\n  file — BufferedFile — the buffered base shared by the channel and SFTP file objects.\n  message — Message — an SSH wire message read or built one typed field at a time.\n  pkey — PKey and PublicBlob — the base key type and raw public-key blobs.\n  proxy — ProxyCommand — a local process used as the transport socket.\n  rsakey — RSAKey — RSA private and public keys.\n  server — Server side: ServerInterface, SubsystemHandler and InteractiveQuery.\n  sftp — SFTP protocol constants and the SFTPError raised on a protocol failure.\n  sftp_attr — SFTPAttributes — the stat record SFTP answers for a remote path.\n  sftp_client — SFTPClient — the client half of SFTP over an open Transport.\n  sftp_file — SFTPFile — one remote file opened over SFTP.\n  sftp_handle — Server side: SFTPHandle — one open file handed back by a SFTPServerInterface.\n  sftp_server — Server side: SFTPServer, the subsystem that serves SFTP over a channel.\n  sftp_si — Server side: SFTPServerInterface — subclass it to answer SFTP requests.\n  ssh_exception — Every failure type: SSHException and its authentication, host-key and channel children.\n  transport — Transport and SecurityOptions — the negotiated session under a client.\n  util — Helpers paramiko exposes: log_to_file, hexify/unhexify, retry_on_signal-style shims.\n\nData:\n  AUTH_FAILED\n  AUTH_PARTIALLY_SUCCESSFUL\n  AUTH_SUCCESSFUL\n  OPEN_FAILED_ADMINISTRATIVELY_PROHIBITED\n  OPEN_FAILED_CONNECT_FAILED\n  OPEN_FAILED_RESOURCE_SHORTAGE\n  OPEN_FAILED_UNKNOWN_CHANNEL_TYPE\n  OPEN_SUCCEEDED\n  SFTP_BAD_MESSAGE\n  SFTP_CONNECTION_LOST\n  SFTP_EOF\n  SFTP_FAILURE\n  SFTP_FLAG_APPEND\n  SFTP_FLAG_CREATE\n  SFTP_FLAG_EXCL\n  SFTP_FLAG_READ\n  SFTP_FLAG_TRUNC\n  SFTP_FLAG_WRITE\n  SFTP_NO_CONNECTION\n  SFTP_NO_SUCH_FILE\n  SFTP_OK\n  SFTP_OP_UNSUPPORTED\n  SFTP_PERMISSION_DENIED\n  io_sleep\n  key_classes\n\nRead one member: doc(\"paramiko.AUTH_FAILED\")"}
