 {:name "pptx", :kind "module", :text "python-pptx-compatible create/open/edit/save backed by one Rust read and one Rust build, including charts, images, rich text, tables, notes, layouts and properties.\n\nClasses:\n  Presentation(pptx=None) — One presentation — slides, slide_layouts, slide_width/height, core_properties, save(path).\n\nModules:\n  api — The Presentation(path=None) entry point — open an existing .pptx or start an empty one.\n  chart — Charts: the chart shape, its data, plots, series, points, markers, axes and labels.\n  dml — Drawing-ML types: fills, lines and colors shared by shapes, text and charts.\n  enum — The enumerations python-pptx exposes for text, shapes, fills and charts.\n  exc — The errors this shim raises: PackageNotFoundError and its InvalidXmlError siblings.\n  presentation — The Presentation object: slides, slide_layouts, slide_width/height, core_properties, save.\n  shapes — Shapes on a slide and the collections that hold them.\n  table — Table, _Row, _Column and _Cell — a table shape and the cells you write into.\n  text — Rich text: a text frame, its paragraphs, their runs and the font on each.\n  util — Length units — Emu, Inches, Pt, Cm, Mm, Centipoints — and the Length base they share.\n\nRead one member: doc(\"pptx.Presentation\")"}
