 {:name "requests", :kind "module", :text "`requests`-compatible API over stdlib urllib. No HTTP/2 or real pooling; `verify=`/`cert=` build the TLS context from a str, bytes or os.PathLike path and `REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE`/`CURL_CA_BUNDLE` are read unless `Session.trust_env` is off; `HTTPDigestAuth` is accepted but sends no auth header.\n\nClasses:\n  CaseInsensitiveDict(data=None) — Case-insensitive header mapping: `headers['content-type']` finds a header sent as `Conte…\n  ChunkedEncodingError(*args, response=None, request=None) — The chunked body ended early or was malformed.\n  ConnectTimeout(*args, response=None, request=None) — The connection was not established within the connect timeout.\n  ConnectionError(*args, response=None, request=None) — The connection could never be established — DNS, refused, or TLS failure.\n  ContentDecodingError(*args, response=None, request=None) — The body could not be decompressed with the encoding the response declared.\n  FileModeWarning(...) — Warned when a file opened in text mode is used as a request body.\n  HTTPError(*args, response=None, request=None) — A 4xx/5xx answer raised by `Response.raise_for_status()`; carries `.response`.\n  InvalidHeader(*args, response=None, request=None) — A header name or value was not valid; also a `ValueError`.\n  InvalidJSONError(*args, response=None, request=None) — The `json=` argument could not be encoded.\n  InvalidProxyURL(*args, response=None, request=None) — The proxy URL was not usable.\n  InvalidSchema(*args, response=None, request=None) — The URL scheme is not one this shim speaks (only http and https); also a `ValueError`.\n  InvalidURL(*args, response=None, request=None) — The URL could not be parsed; also a `ValueError`.\n  JSONDecodeError(*args, response=None, request=None) — `Response.json()` was called on a body that is not JSON; also a `ValueError`.\n  MissingSchema(*args, response=None, request=None) — The URL had no scheme — write `https://host`, not `host`; also a `ValueError`.\n  PreparedRequest() — The fully rendered request that was sent: `method`, `url`, `headers`, `body`. Available …\n  ProxyError(*args, response=None, request=None) — A proxy refused or failed the connection.\n  ReadTimeout(*args, response=None, request=None) — The server sent nothing within the read timeout.\n  Request(method=None, url=None, headers=None, files=None, data=None, params=None, auth=None, cookies=None, json=None, **kw) — A request before it is prepared: method, url, headers, params, data, json, auth; `.prepa…\n  RequestException(*args, response=None, request=None) — Base class of every requests error; catch it to catch both transport failures and `raise…\n  RequestsCookieJar(...) — Cookie jar that also behaves like a dict: `jar['session']`, `.get(name, default)`, `.set…\n  RequestsDependencyWarning(...) — Warned when a dependency version is not the one requests expects.\n  RequestsWarning(...) — Base class of every warning this module raises.\n  Response() — The answer to a request: `status_code`, `headers`, `text`, `content`, `json()`, `ok`, `u…\n  RetryError(*args, response=None, request=None) — Retries were exhausted without a usable answer.\n  SSLError(*args, response=None, request=None) — TLS failed — certificate verification, handshake or protocol.\n  Session() — Reusable session holding headers, cookies, auth, proxies and redirect policy across call…\n  StreamConsumedError(*args, response=None, request=None) — The streamed body was already consumed — read it once, or keep the content.\n  Timeout(*args, response=None, request=None) — Base class of the timeout errors: connect and read.\n  TooManyRedirects(*args, response=None, request=None) — Redirects kept going past the limit; raised only when `allow_redirects=True`.\n  URLRequired(*args, response=None, request=None) — A URL was required and none was given.\n  UnrewindableBodyError(*args, response=None, request=None) — A retried request could not rewind its body, so it was not sent again.\n