 {:name "ruff", :kind "module", :text "In-process Ruff, no pip or PATH: `python -m ruff check|format <paths>` (`--fix`, `--check`, `--diff`) and the `format_/check_/fix_{str,file}` import API, honouring the nearest config per file. A reduced in-process shim, not a full Ruff wheel.\n\nClasses:\n  RuffError(...) — A ruff failure: unknown selector, bad configuration, unparsable source.\n\nFunctions:\n  check_file(path, config=None, **kwargs) — Lint one file on disk with its own discovered configuration.\n  check_str(source, path=None, config=None, line_length=0, select=None, ignore=None, preview=False) — Lint Python `source`, returning a list of diagnostic dicts.\n  config_for(path) — Nearest ruff configuration file governing `path`, or None.\n  console_main(argv=None) — `vis-agent python -m ruff ...` entry point. Returns a process exit code.\n  fix_file(path, config=None, write=True, **kwargs) — Apply Ruff fixes to one file. Returns (changed, fixed_source).\n  fix_str(source, path=None, config=None, line_length=0, select=None, ignore=None, preview=False, unsafe_fixes=False) — Apply Ruff's safe fixes, plus unsafe fixes when explicitly enabled.\n  format_file(path, config=None, write=True, line_length=0) — Format one file on disk. Returns (changed, formatted_source).\n  format_str(source, path=None, config=None, line_length=0) — Format Python `source`, returning the reformatted text.\n  iter_files(paths, explicit_config=None) — Every Python file under `paths`, honoring Ruff excludes for directory targets.\n  main(argv=None) — `vis-agent python -m ruff ...` entry point. Returns a process exit code.\n  version() — `ruff X.Y.Z (vis shim, clj-ruff A.B.C)` -- ruff's own version first,\n\nRead one member: doc(\"ruff.RuffError\")"}
