 {:name "sqlite3", :kind "module", :text "JVM xerial sqlite-jdbc `sqlite3` DB-API 2.0; connections use integer handles. Bindings support int/float/str/None only, else `InterfaceError`.\n\nClasses:\n  Connection(database) — A live database handle: `execute`, `executemany`, `cursor`, `commit`, `rollback`, `close…\n  Cursor(connection) — Iterates one statement's result rows: `execute`, `fetchone`, `fetchall`, `fetchmany`, `r…\n  DataError(...) — A value was out of range or of a type the column cannot hold.\n  DatabaseError(...) — The database rejected the operation; base class of the five errors below.\n  Error(...) — Base class of every error this shim raises; catch it to catch them all.\n  IntegrityError(...) — A constraint failed: UNIQUE, NOT NULL, CHECK or a foreign key.\n  InterfaceError(...) — The database interface itself was misused — a closed connection or cursor, or a bad argu…\n  InternalError(...) — The database reported an internal inconsistency.\n  NotSupportedError(...) — The requested feature is not implemented by this shim.\n  OperationalError(...) — The database could not carry the operation out — a missing file, a locked database, a ba…\n  ProgrammingError(...) — The SQL or its parameters were wrong — an unknown table or column, or a parameter count …\n  Row(cursor, values) — One result row, indexable by position and by column name, and convertible with `dict(row…\n  Warning(...) — Base class for DB-API warnings raised by this shim.\n\nFunctions:\n  complete_statement(sql) — True when `sql` looks like a complete statement, i.e. it ends with a semicolon.\n  connect(database=':memory:', timeout=5.0, detect_types=0, isolation_level='', check_same_thread=True, factory=None, cached_statements=128, uri=False, **kw) — Open a database and return a `Connection`. `database` is a path or `:memory:`; the remai…\n  enable_callback_tracebacks(*a, **k) — Accepted and ignored — this shim has no user-callback layer whose tracebacks could be pr…\n  register_adapter(*a, **k) — Accepted and ignored — this shim stores Python values through its own binder, so no adap…\n  register_converter(*a, **k) — Accepted and ignored — column values come back with their declared SQLite type, so no co…\n\nData:\n  LEGACY_TRANSACTION_CONTROL\n  PARSE_COLNAMES\n  PARSE_DECLTYPES\n  apilevel\n  paramstyle\n  sqlite_version\n  sqlite_version_info\n  threadsafety\n  version\n  version_info\n\nRead one member: doc(\"sqlite3.Connection\")"}
