 {:name "urllib3", :kind "module", :text "`urllib3` as a package: `PoolManager`/`ProxyManager`, `HTTPResponse`, `request`, `util`, `fields`, `filepost`, `exceptions`. TLS options reach the socket and a bad certificate raises `exceptions.SSLError`; retries and pooling are best-effort no-ops. Not supported: `assert_fingerprint`, `ciphers` (`NotImplementedError`).\n\nClasses:\n  BaseHTTPResponse() — urllib3.response.BaseHTTPResponse -- the response base class.\n  HTTPConnectionPool(host, port=None, headers=None, **kw) — One host's connection pool: `request`/`urlopen` against a fixed host, port and scheme.\n  HTTPError(...) — Base class of every urllib3 error the shim raises -- catch this to catch them all.\n  HTTPHeaderDict(data=None, **kw) — Case-insensitive header mapping; repeated keys join with \", \".\n  HTTPResponse(rr) — One HTTP response: `status`, `reason`, `headers`, `data`, `read`, `json`.\n  HTTPSConnectionPool(host, port=443, **kw) — HTTPS pool: an `HTTPConnectionPool` whose scheme is https and whose default port is 443.\n  MaxRetryError(...) — Raised when a request exhausts its retries; carries the pool and the URL that failed.\n  PoolManager(num_pools=10, headers=None, **kw) — The urllib3 entry point: `request`/`urlopen` against any URL, with shared headers and TL…\n  ProxyManager(proxy_url, num_pools=10, headers=None, proxy_headers=None, **_ignored) — Records the proxy and otherwise behaves like a PoolManager: the sandbox\n  Retry(total=10, connect=None, read=None, redirect=None, status=None, backoff_factor=0, status_forcelist=None, **_ignored) — Retry policy: counts and a backoff factor are recorded, never applied -- the shim never …\n  Timeout(total=None, connect=None, read=None) — urllib3.util.Timeout: a total, or a connect/read split.\n  Url(scheme=None, auth=None, host=None, port=None, path=None, query=None, fragment=None) — urllib3.util.Url: the seven parsed URL parts, in order.\n\nFunctions:\n  add_stderr_logger(level=None) — Accepts real code's debug-logging setup and does nothing; the sandbox has no urllib3 log…\n  connection_from_url(url, **kw) — Answers a connection pool bound to that URL's host, scheme and port.\n  disable_warnings(category=None) — Silences the shim's security warnings -- the very call real code makes\n  encode_multipart_formdata(fields, boundary=None) — Encodes `fields` as multipart/form-data, like urllib3.filepost.\n  make_headers(keep_alive=None, accept_encoding=None, user_agent=None, basic_auth=None, proxy_basic_auth=None, disable_cache=None) — Builds a request header dict, like urllib3.util.make_headers.\n  parse_url(url) — Parses `url` into a `Url`, like urllib3.util.parse_url.\n  proxy_from_url(url, **kw) — Answers a `ProxyManager` for that proxy URL; the proxy is recorded, never dialled.\n  request(method, url, **kw) — Performs one request through a throwaway `PoolManager` -- `urllib3.request(\"GET\", url)`.\n\nModules:\n  connectionpool — `HTTPConnectionPool` / `HTTPSConnectionPool`, one host's pool.\n  exceptions — Every urllib3 error class: `HTTPError` and its `PoolError`, `TimeoutError`, `SSLError`, …\n  fields — `RequestField`, one part of a multipart form -- name, data, filename, headers.\n  filepost — Multipart encoding: `encode_multipart_formdata(fields)` -> `(body, content_type)`.\n  poolmanager — `PoolManager` and `ProxyManager`, the two objects that issue requests.\n  response — `HTTPResponse` and `BaseHTTPResponse`: status, headers and an already-buffered body.\n  util — URL parsing (`parse_url`, `Url`), `Retry`, `Timeout` and TLS helpers.\n\nRead one member: doc(\"urllib3.BaseHTTPResponse\")"}
