 {:name "xlsxwriter", :kind "module", :text "Rust-backed `xlsxwriter` .xlsx writer: model the workbook in Python, built on close. Not supported: `constant_memory` streaming, VBA, charts, data validation.\n\nClasses:\n  Format(props=None) — Cell format returned by Workbook.add_format: bold, italic, number format, alignment.\n  Workbook(filename=None, options=None) — Create an .xlsx file at `path`: add_worksheet() sheets, add_format() formats, then close…\n  Worksheet(wb, index, name) — Worksheet: write, write_row, write_column, set_column and freeze_panes into one sheet of…\n  XlsxWriterException(...) — Base error raised by this xlsxwriter subset.\n\nModules:\n  exceptions — xlsxwriter.exceptions: XlsxWriterException, the base error this shim raises.\n  format — xlsxwriter.format: the Format cell-format object a workbook hands out.\n  utility — xlsxwriter.utility: xl_rowcol_to_cell and the other A1/rowcol cell-reference helpers.\n  workbook — xlsxwriter.workbook: the Workbook object that creates worksheets and saves the .xlsx file.\n  worksheet — xlsxwriter.worksheet: the Worksheet object that writes cells, rows and columns.\n\nRead one member: doc(\"xlsxwriter.Format\")"}
