 {:name "yaml", :kind "module", :text "PyYAML-compatible `yaml` via pure-Clojure YAMLStar (YAML 1.2). Map keys return as strings; no custom tags, `!!python` or arbitrary-object (de)serialization.\n\nClasses:\n  YAMLError(...) — Raised when a document cannot be parsed or a value cannot be emitted — the one error typ…\n\nFunctions:\n  dump(data, stream=None, Dumper=None, **kwargs) — Serialize one Python value to a YAML string, or write it to `stream` and return None. `D…\n  dump_all(documents, stream=None, Dumper=None, **kwargs) — Serialize a sequence of Python values as a multi-document YAML stream, separated by `---`.\n  full_load(stream) — Parse one YAML document; an alias of `safe_load` here, because no loader ever constructs…\n  full_load_all(stream) — Iterate every document of a multi-document stream; an alias of `safe_load_all`.\n  load(stream, Loader=None) — Parse the FIRST YAML document of `stream` (str, bytes or a file object) into Python data…\n  load_all(stream, Loader=None) — Iterate every YAML document in a multi-document stream, yielding one Python value per `-…\n  safe_dump(data, stream=None, **kwargs) — Serialize one Python value to YAML; identical to `dump`, since this emitter never writes…\n  safe_dump_all(documents, stream=None, **kwargs) — Serialize a sequence of values as a multi-document YAML stream; identical to `dump_all`.\n  safe_load(stream) — Parse one YAML document safely — the only parse this shim has; identical to `load`.\n  safe_load_all(stream) — Iterate every document of a multi-document stream safely; identical to `load_all`.\n  unsafe_load(stream) — Parse one YAML document. NOT unsafe here: it is the same safe parse as `load` — no Pytho…\n  unsafe_load_all(stream) — Iterate every document of a multi-document stream; the same safe parse as `load_all`.\n\nRead one member: doc(\"yaml.YAMLError\")"}
